From: Athena Build <athena@local>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: gencontrol: default release_prefix to '' for unknown distributions
Origin: vendor
Bug-Athena: thor codename not recognised by debian/bin/gencontrol.py
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-18

debian/bin/gencontrol.py's _generate_abiname_part() hard-codes the
list of recognised distribution codenames (UNRELEASED / bookworm /
bullseye / buster / stretch) and asserts False on anything else.

Athena-Build's _changelog_bump writes `Distribution: thor` (our
release codename), which fails the assert:

    AssertionError: cannot generate ABI name for thor
    make[1]: *** [debian/rules:131: debian/control-real] Error 1
    make: *** [debian/rules:125: debian/control] Error 2

Fix: replace the assert with a fall-through that defaults the
release_prefix to '' (same as bookworm — no codename prefix in the
ABI name).  Keeps the kernel ABI name simple — `-NN` — without
per-codename patch refreshes when Thor's release codename rolls.
The five named distributions still resolve to their original
prefixes on match (the for-loop break path is untouched); only the
else: clause (no match found) is affected.

Python for-else semantics: the else: block runs when the loop
completes without break.  Setting release_prefix in else: overrides
whatever last-iteration value was left behind (Python loop
variables persist after the loop body), giving the intended
default.
---
 debian/bin/gencontrol.py | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/debian/bin/gencontrol.py
+++ b/debian/bin/gencontrol.py
@@ -625,7 +625,9 @@
             if self.changelog[0].distribution.startswith(release_name):
                 break
         else:
-            assert False, f'cannot generate ABI name for {self.changelog[0].distribution}'
+            # Athena-Build: default to bookworm-style prefix (none) for
+            # unknown distributions (e.g. thor).  See patch header.
+            release_prefix = ''

         # Paste that all together
         result = f'-{release_prefix}{abiname_major}'
